Simplified Notes

Why convert at all
- PyTorch needs a Python/framework runtime → doesn't exist on-chip.
- NPUs are power-efficient ASICs, but only run their own compiled format (.bin for QNN, .dlc for SNPE, .pte for ExecuTorch).
- Quantization (int8/int4 — the actual speed/power win) happens during this conversion, not after.


The pipeline
PyTorch/ONNX (dynamic shapes OK)
   ↓ trace/export — SHAPES MUST BECOME STATIC HERE
Qualcomm converter (+ quantization)
   ↓
.bin (QNN) / .dlc (SNPE) / .pte (ExecuTorch)
   ↓
on-device runtime (qnn-net-run / snpe-net-run) — dispatches ops NPU vs CPU fallback

QUAD's own 4-step flow, each step feeding the next:
convert_model → profile_workload → orchestrate_workload → generate_code
   (compile)      (measure)          (allocate for          (emit deployable
                                       power/perf tradeoff)    code/config)
